From: htrecomp
Subject: [PATCH] ui: iterate ImDrawData::CmdLists.Size, not CmdListsCount

ImDrawData::CmdListsCount has been obsolete since Dear ImGui 1.89.8 and is
not maintained by the normal render path. Only the public AddDrawList()
helper updates it; ImGui::Render() populates CmdLists through
AddDrawListToDrawDataEx, and SetupViewportDrawData resets the counter to 0.
The loop therefore never executed a single iteration, so every overlay
(F3 debug, F4 advanced, F5 settings, F6 fps, backtick console) rendered
nothing at all while ImGui reported real geometry:

    CmdListsCount = 0        <- what was iterated
    CmdLists.Size = 1        <- the real count
    TotalVtxCount = 1284     <- geometry was there all along

This is an upstream bug introduced by an ImGui version bump, not a
game-specific workaround. Still present as of rexglue-sdk v0.10.0.

See SDK_PATCHES.md item 2.
---
 src/ui/imgui_drawer.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ui/imgui_drawer.cpp b/src/ui/imgui_drawer.cpp
--- a/src/ui/imgui_drawer.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/imgui_drawer.cpp
@@ -450,7 +450,7 @@
 
   immediate_drawer_->Begin(ui_draw_context, io.DisplaySize.x, io.DisplaySize.y);
 
-  for (int i = 0; i < data->CmdListsCount; ++i) {
+  for (int i = 0; i < data->CmdLists.Size; ++i) {
     const auto cmd_list = data->CmdLists[i];
 
     ImmediateDrawBatch batch;
